      },
      "message": "fix(verify): hole-wall excuse credits tessellation only, not a polygon's flats\n\nThe containment kinds' solid law excused a hole-wall facet by its full\nchord dip into the swept disc, so a coarse polygon hole's flats (an\noctagon's dip ~0.4-0.7 mm) passed a gouge silently. chord_dip now\ncredits at most HOLE_CHORD_CREDIT = DEV_TOL (0.01 mm), the mesh\ntolerance a round wall's tessellation stands within; a deeper dip is\nreal material and convicts.\n\nPinned by hole_wall_chord: octagon and 16-gon holes cut to their corner\ncircle by a drill, a bore orbit and a thread helix convict; a 96-gon\nround hole stays clean for all three.\n\nFixes #1217\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
