      "message": "fix(verify): excuse a hole wall's full chord dip only on a declared rim\n\nCapping every chord-dip credit at the mesh tolerance alone false-gouged\ncoarse round holes that the operation declared (a recognized 16-gon r 2\ndrill hole, the 32-gon drill_plate and tap_plate goldens). The excuse\nnow works edge by edge. An edge with both ends on a declared rim circle\n(the op's hole circles, plus a drill cycle's own diameter at the hole\ncentre) keeps its whole dip, because it is a chord of the round wall\nthe region judges. Any other edge gets at most DEV_TOL, so a polygon's\nflats off the declared rim are judged (the issue's thread at r 4.4 on\nan octagon with corners at r 5).\n\nNew: verify::HoleRim and verify::solid_hits_rims. solid_hits passes no\nrims, so the cross-drill and probe laws get only the capped credit.\ngenerate::contain_into builds the rims from Drill/Bore/Thread holes.\n\nRefs #1217\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
